Prop.Eq.Title=Tone
; The five bands are named by their frequency, because with five of them there
; is no honest word for 1800 Hz and the number is what is being chosen. Only the
; top one gets a word, because a shelf behaves differently from a bell: it lifts
; or lowers EVERYTHING above it, and that is audible as such. {0} is "5 kHz".
Prop.Eq.Shelf={0} and above
; The last cell holds TWO subjects, so the group name has to cover both and
; each switch carries its own. They belong together because they FIGHT: one
; lifts the quiet passages, the other pushes them down, and the quiet passage is
; the pause. The cells also read the signal chain in order, and the gate acts
; last -- so the last cell is where it goes.
Prop.Loudness.Title=Loudness and pauses
Prop.Normalize.Title=Automatic loudness
; Not "noise gate": the reader is being asked about a symptom they can hear, not
; about the name of a filter. It only ever acts where the voice is not.
Prop.Gate.Title=Noise in pauses
